# Image build context: an ALLOWLIST. Everything is excluded, then only what the
# first-party Dockerfiles (infra/docker/*/Dockerfile) read is re-included.
# Dialect is restricted on purpose (scripts/guards/simple/validate-docker-context.sh
# enforces it and scans every admitted file for key material / secret files):
#   `*` first; `!<literal path>` to include; `**/<dir name>/` to exclude below.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.cargo/
!crates/
!proto/
!migrations/
**/target/
# Root-`exclude` fuzz workspaces: no image builds or reads them, and locally they hold
# untracked, generated content the build context would otherwise ship and that
# validate-docker-context scans: the generated EdDSA JWT seed (fuzz/corpus/jwt_validation/),
# libFuzzer corpora and crash artifacts.
**/fuzz/
**/node_modules/
